    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under load, fails predictably, and produces trustworthy performance measurements. It assumes a cluster of N nodes, each running one or more serving processes (\"ranks\"), coordinated by a scheduler or orchestrator.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every rank is running the same logical service.\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact hash.** Compute and record a cryptographic hash (SHA-256) of the model weights, tokenizer files, and config files. Verify all ranks report identical hashes at startup. Do not rely on file paths or timestamps \u2014 paths can differ across nodes and timestamps are meaningless for replicated artifacts.\n- [ ] **Version pinning.** Record exact versions of: inference engine, CUDA/ROCm runtime, driver versions, NCCL/HCCL communication library, Python interpreter, and any custom kernels. Diff across all nodes; any mismatch is a finding, not a warning.\n- [ ] **Serving configuration parity.** Compare the effective (post-merge, post-default-fill) configuration on every rank \u2014 not the config file on disk. Include: max context length, max batch size, KV-cache size per rank, quantization settings, sampling defaults, and chat template. Log the effective config at startup and assert equality across ranks programmatically.\n- [ ] **Determinism-relevant settings.** If deterministic decoding is claimed, verify seeds, temperature handling, and any reduction-order settings are identical. Note that tensor-parallel reductions are often non-deterministic across runs; document whether determinism is guaranteed per-request, per-batch, or not at all.\n- [ ] **Tokenizer identity.** Verify tokenizer version and vocabulary hash on every rank. A mismatched tokenizer on one rank in a pipeline-",
